@startuml
title TMFC002 : Product Order Capture & Validation -- eTOM/SID ABE Links

package "TMFC002 - Product Order Capture & Validation" {
  class "L2 - Product Order Management" as L2ProductOrderManagement <<eTOM Business Activity>>
  class "L2 - Customer Order Processing Mgt" as L2CustomerOrderProcessingMgt <<eTOM Business Activity>>
  class "L2 - Selling" as L2Selling <<eTOM Business Activity>>
  class CustomerProductOrder <<SID Data Entity>>
  class ShoppingCart <<SID Data Entity>>
  class SalesQuote <<SID Data Entity>>
}

package "TMFC005 - Product Inventory" {
  class Product <<SID Data Entity>>
}

' Every link below is an eTOM-activity <-> SID-ABE link. Per the image's own
' legend, an arrow from the eTOM activity towards the SID ABE means
' information produced by the activity; the reverse arrow means information
' consumed by the activity. The image draws each of these pairs with an
' arrowhead at both ends (either as one double-headed arrow, or as two
' separate adjacent single-headed arrows -- confirmed by zooming into each
' arrowhead, since several of these paths run close together or cross),
' i.e. both directions hold simultaneously for every pair below. Unlike
' TMFC039's own eTOM-SID diagram, this image has no SID-entity <-> SID-entity
' arrows, so no undefined-legend case applies here.

L2ProductOrderManagement --> CustomerProductOrder : produces
CustomerProductOrder --> L2ProductOrderManagement : is consumed by

CustomerProductOrder --> L2CustomerOrderProcessingMgt : is consumed by
L2CustomerOrderProcessingMgt --> CustomerProductOrder : produces

L2CustomerOrderProcessingMgt --> ShoppingCart : produces
ShoppingCart --> L2CustomerOrderProcessingMgt : is consumed by

ShoppingCart --> L2Selling : is consumed by
L2Selling --> ShoppingCart : produces

L2Selling --> SalesQuote : produces
SalesQuote --> L2Selling : is consumed by

L2CustomerOrderProcessingMgt --> SalesQuote : produces
SalesQuote --> L2CustomerOrderProcessingMgt : is consumed by

' These two cross into the neighbouring TMFC005 package -- Product is owned
' and updated by TMFC005, not TMFC002 (see TMFC002.md section 2.2's own
' footnote), but this diagram still shows both TMFC002 activities reading
' from / producing into it.
L2ProductOrderManagement --> Product : produces
Product --> L2ProductOrderManagement : is consumed by

L2CustomerOrderProcessingMgt --> Product : produces
Product --> L2CustomerOrderProcessingMgt : is consumed by

legend right
  eTOM Business Activity = dashed-outline rectangle in source image
  SID Data Entity = cylinder in source image
  --> "produces" = eTOM activity to SID ABE arrow
  --> "is consumed by" = SID ABE to eTOM activity arrow
endlegend
@enduml
